<title>CHINA: China Jan-May '97 PC sales surge y-on-y 130 pct.</title>
<headline>China Jan-May '97 PC sales surge y-on-y 130 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales of personal computers in China soared 130 percent in the first five months of 1997 to 1.1 million units, the Business News said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Domestic products were winning a greater market share by selling at lower prices than the foreign products, the newspaper said, but did not elaborate.</p>
<p>China's total sales of personal computers were expected to reach three million in 1997, compared with 1.8 million in 1996, official media has reported.</p>
</text>
